{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417164-casting-a-spell-now-and-triggering-the-effect-later","id":1417164,"title":"Casting a spell now and triggering the effect later","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-07T10:18:28-07:00","id":1417164,"title":"Casting a spell now and triggering the effect later","content":"How difficult is it for a mage to cast a spell (potentially taking their time with an extended roll etc.) early on, and set the effect to be triggered by some other circumstance later?<br /> <br /> The corebook (p. 509) lists &quot;Set Time Trigger&quot; as a Time 4 effect, but I can't find a description in the text anywhere so I'm not sure if that means what I'm looking for.<br /> <br /> HDYDT p. 113 talks about contingency trigger effects, which does look like what I wanted, and apparently it requires...Time 4, Entropy 3-5, and possibly also Matter or Life if the trigger is tied to a physical object or living thing? I'm starting to see why people complain about HDYDT overdoing requirements for stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure how difficult something like this <i>should</i> be. If I were STing, I'd be more than a little leery of allowing PCs to just queue up an array of effects they could trigger easily later (since having a small Arete dice pool seems like the biggest weakness mages have), but since magic can do damn near anything it seems like it should be possible. (If I had to make a snap judgment mid-game I'd probably attach a Quintessence cost or something.) On the other hand, I'm not sure how overpowered this sort of thing really is, compared to just casting spells with long durations.<br /> <br /> While I'm on the subject...is there (or should there be) a difference (in terms of required Sphere levels) between casting an effect that triggers some fixed time period later (e.g. &quot;this spell activates in one week's time&quot;) and casting an effect that triggers upon some specific event (e.g. &quot;this spell activates the next time I point at someone and say 'go fuck yourself' in Latin&quot;)? (I notice that in CtD, changelings can do the former with Time 2 and the latter with Time 3, but obviously Spheres are structured differently than Realms.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","user":"Jefepato","date":". 10-07-2020, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T11:10:40-07:00","id":1417168,"title":"","content":"Time 4 can &quot;hang&quot; a spell for a specific amount of time, or until the mage releases the effect early (up to a maximum amount of time based on the power of the effect).<br /> <br /> Entropy lets you condition a spell occurring on external factor so the mage doesn't either have to time it perfectly or control it directly, but it will trigger the first time any such instance happens.<br /> <br /> Life and Matter (and theoretically other Spheres) let you get more specific. Instead of, &quot;the next time I get punched,&quot; you can do, &quot;the next time I get punched by Bob the Hermetic.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's probably higher ranked than it really needs to be though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T11:21:19-07:00","id":1417170,"title":"","content":"Well, if you think about it, you're effectively casting a spell into the future. So fairly high level stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T11:24:41-07:00","id":1417171,"title":"","content":"*The difficulty it's set by the Sphere level and grade of Vulgarity. I would say that, should the spell be Vulgar, one should cast at &quot;Vulgar With Wittnesses&quot; difficulty level if one want's the trigger to work in pressence of sleepers.<br /> <br /> *You need to add successes as if you were casting a spell with a long duration, because it is a spell with a long duration (the trigger itself its a spell that &quot;freezes&quot; in time another spell 'til later)<br /> <br /> *Don't make it cost Quintessence (or, at least, not much): Time Triggers are competing with Prime 2/3 Charms in terms of &quot;saving a spell for latter use&quot;. Because it's already on a prohibitive lvl 4, I think it's OK to have some advantage in that department.<br /> <br /> *Compared with casting spells with a long duration, the advantage lies in spells that you wouldn't want to have active all that time. Like an explosive fireball, or a Vulgar transformation that would give you pattern bleed if you keep it for too long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I'm on the subject...is there (or should there be) a difference (in terms of required Sphere levels) between casting an effect that triggers some fixed time period later (e.g. &quot;this spell activates in one week's time&quot;) and casting an effect that triggers upon some specific event (e.g. &quot;this spell activates the next time I point at someone and say 'go fuck yourself' in Latin&quot;)? </div> </div> </div>The difference it's that you need to add Entropy for the latter. Think of Spheres as adding attributes to your spells: Time controls time, hence you need nothing else to trigger something at a certain point in time. To &quot;spice&quot; the trigger you need to add other Spheres, Entropy being a classic because it relates to happenstance and meaning.<br /> <br /> Personally I think demanding more than 1-2 it's overkill, though (in general, &quot;sensory effects&quot; are at those levels, and that's what you add when you want your spell to &quot;react to something&quot; - higher levels are to actually control/transmute the subject of the Sphere. With Entropy 5 I migth allow a mage to change such triggering conditions, for instance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-07-2020, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T11:31:19-07:00","id":1417175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417164-casting-a-spell-now-and-triggering-the-effect-later#post1417164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT p. 113 talks about contingency trigger effects, which does look like what I wanted, and apparently it requires...Time 4, Entropy 3-5, and possibly also Matter or Life if the trigger is tied to a physical object or living thing? I'm starting to see why people complain about HDYDT overdoing requirements for stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> A lot of what's in HDYDT feels like an overcorrection for a a continual failure to provide much or any technical specificity for over 20 years, across various prior editions.<br /> <br /> At my table, we've always treated causal triggers as inherently possessing a sort of metacognition that would allow it to make &quot;if/then&quot; determinations--however, we've also required that the effect be given &quot;eyes and ears&quot; (so to speak) in the form of other spheres in order to actually gather the data necessary to check for whether the &quot;if&quot; has occurred. In other words, an effect suspended in time and conditioned to go off on the next human being who enters the immediate vicinity (in addition to whatever spheres are necessary to cast the underlying effect to be suspended) Time 4 to suspend the effect and create the condition, and at least Life 1 to differentiate a human being from a squirrel, a light breeze, or nothing. However, we've always held that the mechanism that actually evaluates whether the condition has been met (the logical engine if you will) is a built-in feature of Time 4.<br /> <br /> Formulations other than this always seemed bizarre because it didn't make sense that one of the major capabilities of Time 4 would inherently require at least one other sphere to operate; i.e., it seems asinine that if you want to suspend an effect to slow time (Time 3) so that it goes off in an hour (the determination of which can be made with Time 1), that you would need anything other than <i>just </i>Time. Using Time 4 to set a conditional trigger is functionally useless if you need another power altogether to provide the effect with the basic logic and syntax necessary to know what it's supposed to do.<br /> <br /> The minutiae that inevitably comes up is in determining which elements or conditions of a trigger can be determined by Time 4 &quot;out of the box&quot;, and which elements are prominent or complex enough, or are defined in such precise terms, that they require their own sphere. This is where you can <i>really</i> start to slice the bologna real thin. Per my group's house rules, if you want to have the effect go off the next time a person enters into (or becomes present within) a room, you'd need Life 1 to ascertain the presence of a person (or, Mind 1 or Spirit 1, depending on how you define a &quot;Person&quot;), and <i>either </i>Correspondence 1 to define &quot;the room&quot; in terms of absolute spatial coordinates, <i>or </i>Matter 1 in order to define &quot;being present within the room&quot; as constituting a position relative to the walls, ceiling, or floor. By default, we hold Time 4's &quot;sensory awareness&quot; as equal to that of an average person at a normal, unstrained alertness level (i.e., neither super absorbed into a task, nor exercising some conscious effort to be hyper aware of their surroundings.) And we have another five or six general principles like this one developed over years of evaluating through various use-case scenarios as they came up.<br /> <br /> I digress, where my group draws the lines may or may not work for you; but at a minimum, you can at least be aware of the general category of determinations that will need to be made when you get into the weeds of generating effects with complex conditional elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 10-07-2020, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:26:55-07:00","id":1417184,"title":"","content":"This makes me curious about the &quot;contingent effect&quot; spell.. The one that every mage would obviously like is &quot;If I'm going to die, do X.&quot; Where X is probably &quot;teleport me to my sanctum and heal me&quot; or something along those lines. Something every high level D&amp;D wizard wants too.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of starting down the path of Time 4 to get contingent effects, more or less just for this. I was assuming it would be Time 4 Life 3 Correspondence 3 to do this (Time 4 for the contigent effect, Life 3 to &quot;see me in danger&quot; and &quot;heal&quot;, Correspondence 3 to teleport me home..) Does that sound right? How else would you do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:27:52-07:00","id":1417185,"title":"","content":"It'd actually move basic Time triggers to 3 myself, to keep it in-line with Correspondence (as another way to cast spells on people in the future via encoding them into a space and hitting people that enter), which also means Time triggers aren't out of reach for starting level characters.<br /> <br /> Though having them be even lower wouldn't break anything and would make Time more appealing instead of feeling like a massive tax to get to a utility effect since time travel is so heavily disincentivized and makes up the rest of Time 4 and 5.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417164-casting-a-spell-now-and-triggering-the-effect-later?p=1417184#post1417184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that sound right? How else would you do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd want Entropy in this one if you want it to go off without needing to be conscious or consciously aware of an attack about to fatally hit you. You wouldn't need Life to target yourself, but you'd still need it for adding healing automatically to the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-07-2020, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T17:54:08-07:00","id":1417733,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses. I believe I understand the general concepts.<br /> <br /> As a follow-up: is it possible for a mage to prepare a single effect that can be fired off piecemeal, with multiple &quot;charges?&quot; (For example: an Etherite jury-rigs a ray gun that can fire several times before breaking down.) My first thought is that it seems most fair to assess Paradox &quot;per shot&quot; in a case like this, if it's allowed at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:07:45-07:00","id":1417737,"title":"","content":"The only real way to handle that is via Charms/Gadgets, or maybe Trinkets. Basically, the ray-gun itself would be a prop, and each shot is a magic item itself. The means a limited number of shots, and each would be subject to Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}